# ── EmailJS Configuration ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your real values.
# .env.local is gitignored — NEVER commit real keys to version control.
#
# ── SETUP STEPS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# STEP 1 — Create the email template
#   a. Go to https://dashboard.emailjs.com/admin/templates
#   b. Click "Create New Template"
#   c. Switch to the HTML editor and paste the full contents of
#      client/emailjs-template.html  (the <body> content)
#   d. Set these fields in the template settings panel:
#        Subject   →  New Portfolio Inquiry from {{from_name}}
#        To email  →  mehdimoradzadeh@outlook.com   (your address — NOT a variable)
#        To name   →  Mehdi
#        Reply-To  →  {{from_email}}
#        From name →  Mehdi Moradzadeh Portfolio
#   e. Save and note the Template ID  (e.g. template_xxxxxxx)
#
# STEP 2 — Locate your existing Service ID
#   a. Go to https://dashboard.emailjs.com/admin
#   b. Click your connected email service
#   c. Copy the Service ID  (e.g. service_xxxxxxx)
#
# STEP 3 — Get your Public Key
#   a. Click your avatar (top-right) → Account → API Keys tab
#   b. Copy the Public Key  (e.g. abc123XYZ...)
#
# STEP 4 — Lock down your Public Key (CRITICAL SECURITY STEP)
#   a. Same Account → API Keys page
#   b. Under "Allowed Origins / Domains" add ONLY your live domain:
#        https://yourdomain.com
#      Do NOT add localhost here — it means no one can abuse the key
#      from outside your production site.
#   c. If you need to test locally, temporarily add http://localhost:5173
#      and remove it again before deploying.
#
# STEP 5 — Fill in .env.local (copy of this file)
#   Replace the placeholder values below with your real IDs.
#   Restart the dev server after saving  (npm run dev).
#
# ── SECURITY CHECKLIST ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   ✓  To email is hard-coded in the template — never comes from form input
#   ✓  Reply-To uses {{from_email}} so you can reply directly to the sender
#   ✓  Public Key restricted to your domain only (Allowed Origins)
#   ✓  ContactForm has: honeypot field, 60s cooldown, RFC-5322 email regex,
#      maxLength limits, and script-char blocking on the name field
#   ✓  This file is in .gitignore — keys never reach version control
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=service_xxxxxxx
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=template_xxxxxxx
VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
